# Story 30: Spawning a Humanoid (50s)
# Hook: Create a humanoid from a skill file -- define channels right in the Markdown.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-30-spawning-humanoid.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Start rysh -- we'll spawn a humanoid with a chatbot channel.

[00:04.0 --> 00:06.0]
Double-press Escape to enter prompt mode.

[00:06.0 --> 00:24.0]
Write a skill file with channel config in the frontmatter. The contacts section defines which channels the humanoid uses.

[00:24.0 --> 00:32.0]
##humanoid spawn reads the file and creates the humanoid. Channel configuration is parsed from the frontmatter.

[00:32.0 --> 00:40.0]
##humanoid list shows the new humanoid and its channels.

[00:40.0 --> 00:50.0]
Humanoid spawned -- channels defined, ready to connect.

